WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.406 --> 00:00:08.932
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.232 --> 00:00:14.195
Unit eight: Describing People. In this unit, you will describe what people look like.

4
00:00:15.183 --> 00:00:15.952
Tall.

5
00:00:16.652 --> 00:00:18.559
Tall means more than the usual height.

6
00:00:18.859 --> 00:00:20.510
My uncle is very tall.

7
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:24.141
Your turn. Say: Tall.

8
00:00:26.841 --> 00:00:27.506
Tall.

9
00:00:28.517 --> 00:00:29.216
Short.

10
00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:32.391
Short means less than the usual height or length.

11
00:00:32.691 --> 00:00:34.052
My grandma is short.

12
00:00:34.752 --> 00:00:37.428
Your turn. Say: Short.

13
00:00:40.128 --> 00:00:40.990
Short.

14
00:00:41.983 --> 00:00:42.764
Curly.

15
00:00:43.464 --> 00:00:46.264
Curly means with many round curves, like circles.

16
00:00:46.564 --> 00:00:48.285
She has got curly hair.

17
00:00:48.985 --> 00:00:51.510
Your turn. Say: Curly.

18
00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:54.956
Curly.

19
00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:56.754
Straight.

20
00:00:57.454 --> 00:00:59.384
Straight means not curly or bent.

21
00:00:59.684 --> 00:01:01.776
My sister has long straight hair.

22
00:01:02.476 --> 00:01:05.186
Your turn. Say: Straight.

23
00:01:07.886 --> 00:01:09.038
Straight.

24
00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.248
Glasses.

25
00:01:11.948 --> 00:01:14.424
Glasses means two lenses you wear to see better.

26
00:01:14.724 --> 00:01:16.549
My teacher wears glasses.

27
00:01:17.249 --> 00:01:20.122
Your turn. Say: Glasses.

28
00:01:22.822 --> 00:01:23.893
Glasses.

29
00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:25.687
Beard.

30
00:01:26.387 --> 00:01:29.048
Beard means hair that grows on a man's chin.

31
00:01:29.348 --> 00:01:31.290
Grandpa has got a white beard.

32
00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:34.654
Your turn. Say: Beard.

33
00:01:37.354 --> 00:01:37.972
Beard.

34
00:01:38.983 --> 00:01:39.822
Slim.

35
00:01:40.522 --> 00:01:42.498
Slim means thin in a nice way.

36
00:01:42.798 --> 00:01:45.204
The dancer is tall and slim.

37
00:01:45.904 --> 00:01:48.603
Your turn. Say: Slim.

38
00:01:51.303 --> 00:01:52.095
Slim.

39
00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:54.073
Describe.

40
00:01:54.773 --> 00:01:57.643
Describe means to say what someone or something is like.

41
00:01:57.943 --> 00:01:59.989
Can you describe your best friend?

42
00:02:00.689 --> 00:02:03.550
Your turn. Say: Describe.

43
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:07.217
Describe.

44
00:02:08.217 --> 00:02:10.402
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:10.702 --> 00:02:12.736
Sreypich, can you describe your uncle?

46
00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:17.213
He's tall and slim. He has got short curly hair.

47
00:02:18.517 --> 00:02:19.820
Has he got a beard?

48
00:02:21.117 --> 00:02:23.174
Yes, he has got a small black beard.

49
00:02:24.483 --> 00:02:25.461
And your aunt?

50
00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:29.771
She has got long straight hair, and she wears glasses.

51
00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:34.917
Grammar focus: He and She has got plus adjective plus noun.

52
00:02:35.217 --> 00:02:38.729
He has got curly hair. She has got long, straight hair.

53
00:02:39.029 --> 00:02:43.420
Put the adjective before the noun: long hair, not hair long.

54
00:02:44.417 --> 00:02:47.324
Now read and listen. My Family's Faces.

55
00:02:47.624 --> 00:02:49.728
Everyone in my family looks different.

56
00:02:51.017 --> 00:02:54.653
My uncle is tall and slim, with short curly hair and a beard.

57
00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:59.389
My aunt has got long straight hair, and she wears glasses.

58
00:03:00.683 --> 00:03:03.693
My little brother is short, and he has got a big smile.

59
00:03:04.983 --> 00:03:07.169
Can you describe someone in your family?

60
00:03:08.483 --> 00:03:11.089
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:11.389 --> 00:03:12.727
She blank got long hair.

62
00:03:13.027 --> 00:03:16.135
A, has. B, have. C, is.

63
00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:21.964
The answer is A: has.

64
00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.821
Hair that grows on a man's chin is a blank.

65
00:03:26.121 --> 00:03:29.368
A, beard. B, glasses. C, curl.

66
00:03:33.383 --> 00:03:35.383
The answer is A: beard.

67
00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.093
He has got blank.

68
00:03:38.393 --> 00:03:42.651
A, curly hair. B, hair curly. C, curly hairs.

69
00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:49.276
The answer is A: curly hair.

70
00:03:50.783 --> 00:03:54.330
Now it's your turn to speak. How would you describe your best friend?

71
00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:04.952
My best friend is short and slim. She has got long black hair, and she wears glasses.

72
00:04:05.252 --> 00:04:07.530
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:08.517 --> 00:04:14.269
Great work today! You learned eight new words and he and she has got plus adjective plus noun.

74
00:04:14.569 --> 00:04:19.915
Today's value is respect for differences. Everyone is different, and everyone is special.

75
00:04:20.215 --> 00:04:22.705
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

76
00:04:23.005 --> 00:04:25.448
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

